7. How do you verify a method was never called?
verify(mockUserRepo, never()).delete(any());

8. How do you verify the order of method calls?

InOrder inOrder = inOrder(mockA, mockB);
inOrder.verify(mockA).callFirst();
inOrder.verify(mockB).callSecond();

9. What is a @Spy? When would you use it?
Spy: Partial mock that delegates to a real object unless stubbed.
Use case: When you need to mock only specific methods of a real object.

@Spy List<String> list = new ArrayList<>();
@Test void testSpy() {
    list.add("real");
    doReturn(false).when(list).add("fake"); // Stub one method
    assertTrue(list.add("real")); // Real method
    assertFalse(list.add("fake")); // Stubbed
}

