11. How do you mock static methods?
Use Mockito 5+ with mockStatic:

try (MockedStatic<Utility> mocked = mockStatic(Utility.class)) {
    mocked.when(Utility::generateId).thenReturn("fixed-id");
    assertEquals("fixed-id", Utility.generateId());
}
Legacy: PowerMock (not recommended for new projects).

12. What are any(), eq(), and argThat()?
any(): Matches any argument (e.g., any(User.class)).
eq(): Matches a specific value (e.g., eq(1L)).
argThat(): Custom matcher (e.g., argThat(user -> user.getName().startsWith("A"))).

when(mockUserRepo.findByEmail(any())).thenReturn(new User());
verify(mockUserRepo).save(argThat(user -> user.getId() == 1L));
Integration with JUnit

