15. What are common Mockito anti-patterns?

Over-mocking: Mocking everything (even simple POJOs).
Verifying implementation details: Focus on behavior, not internal calls.
Ignoring argument captors: Use ArgumentCaptor for complex validations.

16. When would you use ArgumentCaptor?
To inspect arguments passed to a mock:

@Captor ArgumentCaptor<User> userCaptor;
@Test void testSaveUser() {
    userService.register("Alice");
    verify(mockUserRepo).save(userCaptor.capture());
    assertEquals("Alice", userCaptor.getValue().getName());
}

17. How would you test a retry mechanism with Mockito?

@Mock PaymentGateway gateway;
@InjectMocks PaymentService paymentService;

@Test
void testRetryOnFailure() {
    when(gateway.process(any()))
        .thenThrow(new RuntimeException())
        .thenReturn("SUCCESS"); // Fails once, then succeeds
    assertEquals("SUCCESS", paymentService.processWithRetry());
    verify(gateway, times(2)).process(any());
}

